hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"232","From Abu Ismail al-Tirmidhi, from Abu Tawbah al-Rabi’ ibn Nafi’ al-Halabi, from Muawiyah ibn Salam, on the authority of Zayd ibn Salam, who told him: That he heard Abu Salam, he said: Abu Asma Al-Rahbi told me, that Thuban the client of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told him, he said: I was He was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when one of the Jewish rabbis came to him and said: Peace be upon you, Muhammad. I pushed him almost immediately. He was struck by her, so he said: Why do you push me? I said: Don't you say, O Messenger of God? The Jew said: We only call him by the name by which his family called him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “My name is Muhammad by which he called me.” My family.” The Jew said: I came to ask you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Would it benefit you if I spoke to you?” He said: I hear with my ears. So she poked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a stick he had and said: “Ask.” Then the Jew said: Where will the people be on the day the earth and the heavens will be changed for another earth? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In the darkness below the bridge.” He said: Who is the first among people to take leave? He said: “The poor immigrants.” He said: What will be their gift when they enter Paradise? He said: “The increase in the liver of the nun.” He said: What is their diet as a result of it? He said: “The bull of Paradise, which used to eat from its outskirts, will be slaughtered for them.” He said: What will they do with it? He said: “From a spring in it called Salsabila.” He said: You are right, and I have come to ask you about something that no one of the people of the earth knows except a prophet or a man or Two men said: “Will it benefit you if I speak to you?” He said: I hear with my ears. He said: “Would it benefit you if I spoke to you?” He said: I hear with my ears. He said: I came. I ask you about the boy. He said: “A man’s semen is white, and a woman’s semen is yellow, so when they come together they make a man’s semen like a woman’s semen.” They mentioned God willing, and when the woman’s semen is superior to the man’s semen, she will be female, God willing.” The Jew said: “You are right, and indeed you are a prophet.” Then he left. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This man asked me about the one he asked me about, and I had no knowledge of any of it until God brought it to me.”"
